</div></section>

<section id="plan"><div class="wrap">
<h2>How I would deliver it</h2>
<div class="steps">
<div class="card">Build a market and competitor overview from public information</div>
<div class="card">Create the dashboard structure and formulas, using labelled sample data</div>
<div class="card">Rank markets by contribution, reorder performance and cost to serve</div>
<div class="card">Request anonymized shipment, sales and cost data to validate the model</div>
<div class="card">Recommend a rollout or capacity decision only after checking actual figures</div>
</div>
<p style="margin-top:24px">I would start with two existing markets under different conditions, such as the home market and a metro or tourism market. Tracked measures: contribution per case, reorder rate, freight per case, active accounts and inventory days.</p>
<div class="note"><b>What I will not claim:</b> a specific rupee profit or sales uplift from public data alone. Internal costs and sell-through determine that. India’s alcohol rules are state-specific and marketing options are limited, so every rollout or trade activation plan must be checked against the relevant state requirements (see the USDA India market report).</div>
</div></section>

